      "body": [
        {
          "type": "TextualBody",
          "value": "\n<ol><li dir=\"ltr\">[...] situated on the shore of the sea</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">[.... of his] own [choice \u2026] to be married to this \u1e24usn, the virgin,\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">[... f]eed and s[upport \u2026 in the manner of Jewish men, who fee]d and support and \u2026 their wives faithfully.</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">[... And \u1e24usn,] the bride, daughter of [Mard\u016bk harkened to] Khalaf, [the groom], b. Ma\u1e25f\u016b\u1e93 (whose) s(oul is at) r(est) (and agreed) to be his wife and to</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">[serve him \u2026 in the m]anner of wives, the daughters of Isra[el, who att]end, show honor, and esteem their husbands in purity and sanctity. And he took</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">[... \u1e24]usn, the virgin, the bride, daughter of Mard\u016bk (whose) s(oul is at) r(est), in complete qiddushin with two hundred zuz, as the holy college had established.</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">[...] The two of them consented, in the presence of trustworthy Jewish men, valid witnesses, that her mohar be thirty-five dinars of pure, good quality gold.\u00a0\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">[...] And he has already presented to her, at the time of her betrothal, five dinars. And there remain incumbent upon him thirty dinars of good quality gold, with the insignia of the temporal ruler.\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">[...He gave] her from his money an Egyptian sheet, an absolute and permanent gift. And this is what she brought from the Merciful and from the house of her fat[hers:]\u00a0\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">[...] dyeing vessel, a water container and a mortar\u2014ten dina[rs ...] </li></ol>\n",
          "format": "text/html"
        }
      ],
